  "id": "psychotherapy-integration",
  "term": "psychotherapy integration",
  "definition": "Psychotherapy integration is the practice of combining elements from different psychotherapy approaches within treatment as it is usually delivered. In this packet, it refers specifically to adding emotion-focused therapy components to an existing therapy approach to better reflect real-world practice.",
